1
00:00:05,367 --> 00:00:11,767
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:32,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:35,133
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,233
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,867
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,067
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,167
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:48,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,667 --> 00:00:51,633
[GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:53,367
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,333
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,567 --> 00:00:57,933
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,067 --> 00:01:00,167
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,067
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:11,600
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:12,800
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,933 --> 00:01:14,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:23,567
<i>Hey, Gabo's useful now!
He's got a job!</i>

21
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:27,000
<i>Who knows, he might slowly
be robbing us of our income.</i>

22
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:28,700
<i> Gabo can't overpower us.</i>

23
00:01:28,833 --> 00:01:30,167
<i>He'll have to deal
with my fists first!</i>

24
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:34,400
<i>Can I borrow the bike again
to get to work?</i>

25
00:01:34,533 --> 00:01:35,900
<i>You promise
you'll take care of it?</i>

26
00:01:36,033 --> 00:01:37,233
<i>- Yes, Pa.
- Alright, then.</i>

27
00:01:37,367 --> 00:01:40,200
<i>Where would you like to eat
once we're done with enrollment?</i>

28
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:43,033
<i> I love you, Mommy.</i>

29
00:01:43,167 --> 00:01:44,700
<i>The restaurant
you love eating at?</i>

30
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:47,233
<i>- Yes, Ma!
- Okay.</i>

31
00:01:49,733 --> 00:01:52,133
<i> She's already suspended,
</i>but there's still an interview?

32
00:01:52,267 --> 00:01:54,400
<i>Sir, remember,
if Sam didn't take action,</i>

33
00:01:54,533 --> 00:01:56,233
<i>we wouldn't have been able
to catch Mr. Chan.</i>

34
00:01:56,367 --> 00:01:59,100
<i>You really came here
to face the consequences?</i>

35
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:00,867
<i>I'm only fulfilling part
of my duty.</i>

36
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,533
This agency would be better off
<i> without you.</i>

37
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:09,800
[ESTRELLA] Ma'am, I'm done
with the report you asked for.

38
00:02:10,267 --> 00:02:12,333
You just need to check it
before we submit it.

39
00:02:13,267 --> 00:02:14,600
Ma'am.

40
00:02:14,767 --> 00:02:15,867
Are you alright?

41
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,467
Not really.

42
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:22,033
The NCIA suspended Sam.

43
00:02:22,167 --> 00:02:23,167
Huh?!

44
00:02:24,033 --> 00:02:26,567
Ma'am Sam?
But she's a good agent!

45
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,433
Why was she suspended?

46
00:02:28,567 --> 00:02:30,933
She punched someone.
The suspect!

47
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:32,567
She even violated
so many protocols,

48
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:35,233
so, now,
Daddy's very stressed out!

49
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:36,367
You know him.

50
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:38,967
He doesn't want
his name tarnished!

51
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:41,333
We already have too much
on our plate...

52
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,633
I don't know
what to do anymore.

53
00:02:43,767 --> 00:02:46,067
I'm still thinking
on how to resolve that.

54
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:50,567
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

55
00:02:50,733 --> 00:02:51,667
[CHAIR SWIVELS]

56
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:52,767
Estrella...

57
00:02:53,567 --> 00:02:55,167
- Come with me.
- Where, ma'am?

58
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,500
To Ginintuang Lupa.

59
00:02:56,633 --> 00:02:58,900
We need to talk
to the man who was shot.

60
00:02:59,033 --> 00:03:01,467
We need to stop him
from suing us.

61
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:03,000
Alright, but, ma'am...

62
00:03:03,133 --> 00:03:06,200
I think we should tell this
to Domingo.

63
00:03:06,333 --> 00:03:07,400
Alright, let's go.

64
00:03:10,733 --> 00:03:14,200
Romy, where's our coffin?

65
00:03:14,333 --> 00:03:18,100
Oh, boss, Miss Maring rented it
for her gambling den.

66
00:03:18,233 --> 00:03:20,900
But we only have
a three-day contract with her.

67
00:03:21,067 --> 00:03:22,333
- Pa!
- Oh?

68
00:03:23,133 --> 00:03:26,500
I thought of a way
to find out Gabo's secret

69
00:03:26,633 --> 00:03:28,967
on how he made that much money.

70
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:31,533
- How?
- I'll use Tolits and Binoy.

71
00:03:31,667 --> 00:03:35,733
But will they talk to you?
They already left our group.

72
00:03:35,867 --> 00:03:37,600
I know those guys very well.

73
00:03:38,433 --> 00:03:39,533
They're gullible.

74
00:03:40,167 --> 00:03:41,333
When we met...

75
00:03:41,467 --> 00:03:44,433
I made them believe I didn't
want to fight Gabo anymore.

76
00:03:44,567 --> 00:03:48,733
Django, you need to talk
to them first...

77
00:03:49,433 --> 00:03:50,733
...before scaring them.

78
00:03:50,867 --> 00:03:54,600
You know those guys are cowards.
They speak so mindlessly.

79
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,333
You can handle them!

80
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:57,967
- Pa!
- Oh?

81
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,667
I just take one look at them...

82
00:04:00,433 --> 00:04:02,567
And I'm sure
they're already scared to death.

83
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:05,967
- What more if I take this out?
- That's what I'm talking about!

84
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:08,833
They might just start peeing!
[LAUGHS]

85
00:04:08,967 --> 00:04:10,267
That's Django for you!

86
00:04:11,367 --> 00:04:12,433
That can happen...

87
00:04:13,167 --> 00:04:16,133
...if you do that job yourself.

88
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:19,367
Copy, Pa.

89
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:21,067
Let's go!

90
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:28,900
Sir.

91
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:31,900
[DOMINGO] Jacinto and
Estrella, what do you want?

92
00:04:33,333 --> 00:04:35,100
Sir, we would like to ask
for permission

93
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:37,167
to visit the family
of the man who was shot

94
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:38,400
during the demolition.

95
00:04:38,533 --> 00:04:41,167
Why? What's the update
on what I asked you to do?

96
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:42,567
That's why
we're going there, sir.

97
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,967
We want to know
what they're planning.

98
00:04:45,100 --> 00:04:49,200
And also to discourage them
from suing NLEA.

99
00:04:49,833 --> 00:04:50,733
Go ahead.

100
00:04:50,867 --> 00:04:53,967
We need to make sure
they won't file a case.

101
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:57,900
I don't want to be surprised
if we fail again.

102
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,467
Copy, sir.

103
00:05:00,233 --> 00:05:02,067
- You may go.
- Thank you, sir.

104
00:05:02,233 --> 00:05:03,133
Thank you, sir.

105
00:05:03,267 --> 00:05:05,767
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

106
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:06,900
[ELTON] Hey, Rudy.

107
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:09,733
Rudy.

108
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:13,433
What exactly is Gabo's job?

109
00:05:13,567 --> 00:05:16,133
He told me
he's a messenger.

110
00:05:16,267 --> 00:05:17,333
Messenger?

111
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:19,967
Tekla!

112
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,600
- Come here.
- What is it, Mister Rudy?

113
00:05:24,567 --> 00:05:26,300
What really is Gabo's job?

114
00:05:26,433 --> 00:05:27,733
[BOTH STUTTERING]

115
00:05:27,867 --> 00:05:29,900
He told you
he's a messenger, right?

116
00:05:30,033 --> 00:05:33,333
- Yes.
- [TEKLA] Trust Gabo, okay?

117
00:05:33,467 --> 00:05:35,633
Don't worry, he won't do
anything bad.

118
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,667
[IPE] That's right, Mister Rudy.
What matters is

119
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:39,367
Gabo has a proper job now.

120
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:42,167
[BONG] Yes, a proper job
with a big pay.

121
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,433
- Elton.
- Hm?

122
00:05:43,567 --> 00:05:45,600
You be in charge for now.
I'll buy my meds.

123
00:05:45,733 --> 00:05:47,033
- Alright.
- We can do it!

124
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:48,667
We're not doing anything today.

125
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:51,467
No, I can manage.
I need to walk around.

126
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,667
- Go on. Yeah, thanks.
- Are you sure?

127
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:55,433
Be careful.

128
00:05:57,933 --> 00:06:00,333
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

129
00:06:00,467 --> 00:06:03,367
[ENGINE REVVING]

130
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:04,667
This is a stickup!
Give me your bag!

131
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:05,767
Give it!

132
00:06:06,867 --> 00:06:07,867
[KID CRYING]

133
00:06:08,033 --> 00:06:09,200
- [WOMAN] Son!
- [THIEF] Stand up!

134
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:11,500
- [WOMAN] My son!
- [THIEF] Give me the bag!

135
00:06:11,633 --> 00:06:13,000
- [KID CRYING]
- [THIEF SHOUTING]

136
00:06:13,133 --> 00:06:14,500
[GUNSHOT]

137
00:06:14,633 --> 00:06:15,667
[KID] Ma!

138
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,300
[ENGINE REVVING]

139
00:06:17,433 --> 00:06:18,700
- [CRYING] Ma!
- Let's go!

140
00:06:18,833 --> 00:06:20,500
- [CRYING] Ma!
- [THIEF] Hurry!

141
00:06:20,633 --> 00:06:22,300
- [GABO] Ahh!
- [ENGINE REVVING]

142
00:06:22,433 --> 00:06:23,300
[BODIES THUD]

143
00:06:23,433 --> 00:06:25,400
- Ahh!
- [ENGINE REVVING]

144
00:06:27,033 --> 00:06:28,400
[CRYING] Help!

145
00:06:28,533 --> 00:06:30,667
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

146
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:33,000
Help! Help!

147
00:06:33,133 --> 00:06:34,267
<i>- Mommy!
- [SMACKS]</i>

148
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:35,400
[GUNSHOT]

149
00:06:36,433 --> 00:06:41,600
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

150
00:06:41,767 --> 00:06:45,000
[BLOWS LANDING]

151
00:06:45,133 --> 00:06:47,233
- [GUNSHOT]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

152
00:06:48,933 --> 00:06:50,000
[KICK LANDS]

153
00:06:50,133 --> 00:06:53,233
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

154
00:06:53,367 --> 00:06:56,033
- [GUNSHOT]
- [BLOWS, KICKS LANDING]

155
00:06:56,167 --> 00:06:58,233
- [KNIFE SWISHES]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

156
00:06:58,367 --> 00:06:59,933
- [KICKS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

157
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:02,133
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

158
00:07:02,267 --> 00:07:03,533
[BODY THUDS]

159
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:04,867
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

160
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,033
- [KICK LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

161
00:07:06,767 --> 00:07:08,033
[CRYING] Ma!

162
00:07:08,167 --> 00:07:09,167
[WOMAN GROANS]

163
00:07:11,467 --> 00:07:12,433
Ma!

164
00:07:13,133 --> 00:07:16,000
Ahh! Ah! Ah!

165
00:07:16,167 --> 00:07:17,867
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

166
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,267
[CRYING] Ma!

167
00:07:19,767 --> 00:07:21,267
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

168
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:22,267
Help!

169
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:25,267
- Ahh! [BREATHING HEAVILY]
- Stop it, sir!

170
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:27,833
Please help my mom!

171
00:07:27,967 --> 00:07:33,767
[KID CRYING]

172
00:07:40,667 --> 00:07:41,833
[CRYING] Ma...

173
00:07:42,867 --> 00:07:43,767
Help!

174
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:46,667
[KID CRYING]

175
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,867
Help us!

176
00:07:49,233 --> 00:07:51,567
Help us! Help us!

177
00:07:54,733 --> 00:07:55,933
You heard Ma'am Pia.

178
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:57,067
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

179
00:07:57,067 --> 00:07:58,600
It turns out...

180
00:07:59,533 --> 00:08:02,367
we could also be dragged into
the investigation of Ma'am Sam.

181
00:08:02,367 --> 00:08:03,633
Does this mean...

182
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:05,833
we might get into trouble
because of Ma'am Sam?

183
00:08:06,933 --> 00:08:08,467
I don't think that's fair.

184
00:08:08,467 --> 00:08:09,933
[BORROMEO]
It would be too unfair.

185
00:08:09,933 --> 00:08:12,433
I have spent years
in the service,

186
00:08:12,733 --> 00:08:14,700
and now it might all be ruined

187
00:08:14,933 --> 00:08:16,433
because of one person.

188
00:08:16,433 --> 00:08:18,133
[KAREN] Guys, we're here now.

189
00:08:18,133 --> 00:08:20,133
Besides, we were all willing
to go along with the plan.

190
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:22,100
- Were any of you forced?
- [ROBERT] Not really.

191
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:23,767
We just went along.

192
00:08:23,767 --> 00:08:25,767
I wasn't forced,
but I felt pressured.

193
00:08:25,767 --> 00:08:27,700
[SEQIOA] I know we've made
a lot of bad choices,

194
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:29,600
but for this one...
We should've stopped!

195
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:30,900
Wait a minute.

196
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:33,367
We knew from the very start that
we'd have to cross some lines

197
00:08:33,367 --> 00:08:34,567
when we agreed to this.

198
00:08:34,567 --> 00:08:36,600
But now, just because
a small problem came up,

199
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,967
we're going to point fingers?

200
00:08:37,967 --> 00:08:39,267
Betray each other?

201
00:08:39,267 --> 00:08:41,867
Team, it's just a little bump
in the road!

202
00:08:41,867 --> 00:08:43,967
We'll get through this!
Pull yourselves together!

203
00:08:43,967 --> 00:08:45,167
I know...

204
00:08:45,167 --> 00:08:47,300
this doesn't necessarily mean
the end of the world.

205
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:50,667
But what about our careers
in the NCIA?

206
00:08:50,667 --> 00:08:51,600
Just like that, gone?

207
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:52,833
Which matters more to you?

208
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:53,833
Your career,

209
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:55,200
or arresting criminals?

210
00:08:55,233 --> 00:08:58,133
Which we did, by the way,
in case you forgot.

211
00:08:58,133 --> 00:08:59,300
Whatever.

212
00:08:59,867 --> 00:09:03,200
If we get into trouble,
let's forget about each other.

213
00:09:03,967 --> 00:09:05,433
What's wrong with you, Reyes?!

214
00:09:05,433 --> 00:09:08,133
We should stick together!
Team Alpha should be solid!

215
00:09:08,133 --> 00:09:10,167
If we were in Ma'am Sam's shoes,

216
00:09:10,167 --> 00:09:11,433
if we were the ones in trouble,

217
00:09:11,433 --> 00:09:13,533
I'm sure she would support us!

218
00:09:13,533 --> 00:09:16,767
That's why we should give her
the same support!

219
00:09:16,767 --> 00:09:17,833
Exactly!

220
00:09:18,333 --> 00:09:19,433
[INAUDIBLE]

221
00:09:19,933 --> 00:09:21,133
Weaklings.

222
00:09:21,133 --> 00:09:26,167
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

223
00:09:26,167 --> 00:09:27,500
[WATER POURING]

224
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,667
Oh! Sir, I didn't see you!

225
00:09:29,667 --> 00:09:30,867
Hey, sir!

226
00:09:30,867 --> 00:09:32,967
- So, how did it go...
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

227
00:09:32,967 --> 00:09:34,133
...driving Ma'am Sam home?

228
00:09:35,067 --> 00:09:36,833
Very good, Rallos.

229
00:09:38,167 --> 00:09:40,467
So, did you get a kiss?

230
00:09:40,467 --> 00:09:42,533
On the cheeks? On the lips?

231
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:44,733
[EXHALES LOUDLY]

232
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:46,933
Even better.

233
00:09:47,267 --> 00:09:48,833
What do you mean?

234
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:51,467
She introduced me
to her parents.

235
00:09:52,167 --> 00:09:53,933
And they loved me!

236
00:09:53,933 --> 00:09:55,600
- Hey, whoa!
- [CHUCKLING]

237
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,733
You're the man, sir!

238
00:09:57,733 --> 00:09:59,300
- The one and only, right?
- So impressive!

239
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:01,833
But, sir, you shouldn't be
satisfied with just one point.

240
00:10:01,867 --> 00:10:03,333
I know. That's why...

241
00:10:03,333 --> 00:10:06,467
I'm trying to convince Delgado
not to fire her.

242
00:10:06,467 --> 00:10:08,167
Hey, that's not just one point.

243
00:10:08,167 --> 00:10:10,467
[CHUCKLES] Absolutely, sir!

244
00:10:10,467 --> 00:10:12,233
Once that happens, sir,

245
00:10:12,233 --> 00:10:13,833
Ma'am Sam will finally
say yes to you.

246
00:10:13,833 --> 00:10:18,667
And honestly, any woman would
fall for a suitor like you.

247
00:10:18,667 --> 00:10:20,200
Once we end up together,

248
00:10:20,633 --> 00:10:23,100
everything I've worked
so hard for...

249
00:10:23,467 --> 00:10:26,133
It'll be all worth it.

250
00:10:26,133 --> 00:10:29,033
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

251
00:10:29,033 --> 00:10:30,633
Guys, it's Ma'am Sam.

252
00:10:31,467 --> 00:10:33,500
[KAREN] Sam, what's up?
Are you okay?

253
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,633
I don't know if I'm okay.

254
00:10:41,067 --> 00:10:42,067
Team.

255
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:44,467
How are you holding up?

256
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:46,800
[ROBERT]
Well, what do you think?

257
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,833
We're all worried.

258
00:10:49,467 --> 00:10:50,833
Because we could be next.

259
00:10:52,467 --> 00:10:53,967
[SEQIOA]
So, you're suspended, huh?

260
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:55,500
What about tomorrow?

261
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:57,033
We might get suspended too.

262
00:10:57,033 --> 00:10:58,600
[BORROMEO] I'd be fine
with only a suspension.

263
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,600
But what if we lost
everything we worked hard for?

264
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:01,867
[KAREN] Are you guys serious?

265
00:11:01,867 --> 00:11:04,433
I thought you already understood
that it wasn't Sam's fault?

266
00:11:04,433 --> 00:11:05,433
[ROBERT] Come on, Karen.

267
00:11:05,433 --> 00:11:08,200
Why can't we just say
what we really feel?

268
00:11:08,233 --> 00:11:10,533
[CASTOR] If it's all going
to end in blame,

269
00:11:10,533 --> 00:11:11,933
you shouldn't have even come!

270
00:11:11,933 --> 00:11:13,367
No one forced you anyway!

271
00:11:13,367 --> 00:11:15,167
[BORROMEO] Sure, but if
we hadn't come along,

272
00:11:15,167 --> 00:11:16,733
you'd call us cowards.

273
00:11:16,733 --> 00:11:17,833
No sense of camaraderie.

274
00:11:17,833 --> 00:11:19,867
When the head tells you to jump,

275
00:11:19,867 --> 00:11:21,633
you are supposed to jump!

276
00:11:21,633 --> 00:11:23,233
Let's not pretend that
we had a choice here.

277
00:11:23,233 --> 00:11:24,533
Because we didn't have any!

278
00:11:24,533 --> 00:11:26,533
Are we really blaming each
other right in front of Sam?!

279
00:11:26,533 --> 00:11:27,633
Enough.

280
00:11:28,333 --> 00:11:29,533
That's enough, please.

281
00:11:29,533 --> 00:11:31,167
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

282
00:11:31,167 --> 00:11:32,233
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

283
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:33,433
I'm sorry.

284
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:35,800
It's all on me.

285
00:11:38,033 --> 00:11:41,700
I'm asking for your forgiveness,
not as your team leader...

286
00:11:42,367 --> 00:11:45,633
not as a colleague whose actions
have affected your careers.

287
00:11:46,467 --> 00:11:48,467
I'm asking for your
forgiveness as...

288
00:11:49,067 --> 00:11:50,667
as your friend.

289
00:11:50,667 --> 00:11:52,267
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

290
00:11:52,267 --> 00:11:54,267
I'm sorry. I let you all down.

291
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:58,100
I came here today to explain
to the Internal Affairs people

292
00:11:58,100 --> 00:12:01,400
that all of this chaos was
caused by me alone.

293
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,800
I'm the only one at fault,

294
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:06,400
and it's my responsibility
to face the consequences.

295
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:09,500
Sam, you don't need
to apologize.

296
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:11,100
We knew what
we were getting into.

297
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:12,500
Karen is right, Ma'am Sam.

298
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:14,600
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

299
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:15,900
I'm sorry, Ma'am Sam.

300
00:12:16,333 --> 00:12:17,733
We just panicked.

301
00:12:17,733 --> 00:12:21,133
We're just worried
about our families and our jobs.

302
00:12:29,133 --> 00:12:30,133
[GABO] Help!

303
00:12:30,633 --> 00:12:32,833
- Help! Help us!
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

304
00:12:32,833 --> 00:12:34,167
Quick, help us!

305
00:12:34,167 --> 00:12:35,933
- [DOCTOR] What happened?
- She was shot.

306
00:12:35,933 --> 00:12:37,767
- Take her straight to Trauma!
- Mama...

307
00:12:37,767 --> 00:12:41,133
- [WHEELS RATTLING]
- [SOBBING]

308
00:12:41,133 --> 00:12:42,133
Mama!

309
00:12:42,667 --> 00:12:43,833
Sir, this is as far
as you can go.

310
00:12:43,833 --> 00:12:44,933
Please proceed
to the information table...

311
00:12:44,933 --> 00:12:46,533
- Mama...
- ...for the patient's details.

312
00:12:46,533 --> 00:12:51,333
- [SOBBING CONTINUES]
- [MUSIC FADING]

313
00:12:51,367 --> 00:12:52,333
[GABO] Miss...

314
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:55,400
H-He's the son
of the gunshot victim.

315
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,833
What is the name of the victim?

316
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:58,000
[SOBS] Linda.

317
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,667
Linda Reyes.

318
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,200
How are you related
to the victim, sir?

319
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:03,900
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

320
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:05,800
Miss, I'm not a relative.

321
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:08,900
I just happened to pass by
and rescued them.

322
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:10,700
Then I brought them here
to the hospital.

323
00:13:11,633 --> 00:13:13,233
[GOON] You got the wrong guy!

324
00:13:13,233 --> 00:13:14,800
- [COP 1] Don't resist!
- [COP 2] Come with us!

325
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:16,000
- [CAR DOOR SLIDING]
- [CAR DOOR OPENS]

326
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,133
- Oli, stay sharp.
- Copy that.

327
00:13:17,133 --> 00:13:18,800
- Just remain vigilant.
- I'll start filming now.

328
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:20,433
- Shoot this scene.
- [MAN 1] Look, it's him!

329
00:13:20,433 --> 00:13:21,700
- My idol.
- Over here.

330
00:13:21,733 --> 00:13:23,733
- [MAN 2] I'm your fan!
- [WOMAN 1] One selfie, please!

331
00:13:23,733 --> 00:13:25,233
- [PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

332
00:13:25,233 --> 00:13:27,333
- We're rolling now, Salvador.
- What happened here?

333
00:13:27,333 --> 00:13:28,667
A robbery took place here,

334
00:13:28,667 --> 00:13:30,267
and a woman got shot.

335
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:31,467
How's the victim?
Where is she?

336
00:13:31,467 --> 00:13:33,600
She was rushed
to Bernardino Hospital.

337
00:13:33,867 --> 00:13:35,667
Good thing you caught
the robbers.

338
00:13:35,667 --> 00:13:37,133
- Not us.
- [OLI] Huh?

339
00:13:37,133 --> 00:13:38,733
A man fought back against them.

340
00:13:38,733 --> 00:13:40,833
He also helped
the victim and her child.

341
00:13:40,833 --> 00:13:42,833
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

342
00:13:42,833 --> 00:13:43,833
Thank you, man.

343
00:13:43,833 --> 00:13:45,133
No story here,
let's head to the hospital.

344
00:13:45,133 --> 00:13:46,333
- Thanks, Chief.
- Thank you, thank you.

345
00:13:46,333 --> 00:13:48,233
- My idol!
- Let's take a picture!

346
00:13:48,233 --> 00:13:49,867
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]
- Thank you!

347
00:13:49,867 --> 00:13:51,667
[OLI] Sorry, we're in a hurry.

348
00:13:51,667 --> 00:13:53,400
- [SOBBING]
- Uh, kid...

349
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:56,167
Do you know the cell phone
numbers of any relatives

350
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,300
we can contact?

351
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:58,633
No, sir.

352
00:13:58,633 --> 00:14:03,133
Our phone was inside the bag
that was stolen from us.

353
00:14:03,133 --> 00:14:04,600
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,300
Uh, miss, I'm sorry.

355
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:07,800
I have a favor.

356
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:10,800
Please do everything you can
to save his mother's life.

357
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:11,800
Yes, sir.

358
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:14,600
We'll do our very best
for the child

359
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:15,700
and the victim.

360
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:20,533
Sir, will my mother survive?

361
00:14:20,533 --> 00:14:23,100
Will she live?

362
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:24,633
[SOBBING CONTINUES]

363
00:14:24,633 --> 00:14:31,600
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

364
00:14:57,867 --> 00:15:02,367
[MUSIC SWELLING]

365
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:05,833
[DABOY] It's afternoon now,

366
00:15:05,833 --> 00:15:07,733
and we still haven't earned
money for Gabo.

367
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:11,667
Even if we look for a job,
we won't get hired.

368
00:15:11,667 --> 00:15:13,100
We don't know how
to do anything else.

369
00:15:13,467 --> 00:15:15,600
What if we go back
to what we used to do?

370
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:16,800
What do you mean?

371
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,000
Snatching. Stealing.
Pickpocketing.

372
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,100
Easy money!

373
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:22,033
Hey, don't.

374
00:15:22,033 --> 00:15:24,300
Didn't we promise Gabo we
wouldn't do anything bad again?

375
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:26,467
Why? Will he find out?
Are you going to tell him?

376
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:29,800
Even so, we can still earn
in a good way.

377
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:32,033
There.

378
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,400
That's how we'll make money.

379
00:15:35,033 --> 00:15:35,967
How?

380
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:38,133
I'm good at Chinese Poker. You?

381
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:39,600
[BINOY] Tonk.

382
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:40,600
[TOLITS] How about you?

383
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:42,300
I'm good
at the Monkey Card Game.

384
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:44,300
- The draw-and-guess one.
- That suits you.

385
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:45,733
You look like a monkey.
Let's go.

386
00:15:45,733 --> 00:15:47,333
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

387
00:15:47,333 --> 00:15:48,300
I'll sit here.

388
00:15:50,467 --> 00:15:52,433
- So, did you find them?
- Boss.

389
00:15:52,433 --> 00:15:54,200
They're not at their usual
hangout spot.

390
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:57,267
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

391
00:15:57,267 --> 00:15:58,433
[DJANGO SIGHS]

392
00:15:58,433 --> 00:16:00,800
Where else could those
three bastards be hanging out?

393
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:04,100
What about our gambling spot
at Miss Maring's?

394
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:06,267
- Did you check that?
- Not yet, boss.

395
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:10,500
- [HORN HONKING IN DISTANCE]
- [HEAVY FOOTSTEPS]

396
00:16:11,267 --> 00:16:13,367
Hey, let's be generous.

397
00:16:13,967 --> 00:16:14,900
Ah.

398
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:18,700
Miss Maring, our condolences.

399
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:20,267
Miss Maring, do you have
coffee here?

400
00:16:20,267 --> 00:16:21,400
Of course we do!

401
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,567
Uh, can we ask what happened
to Mister...

402
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:26,133
Mister Antonio?

403
00:16:26,133 --> 00:16:28,000
You sound like
you're not from here.

404
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,300
Obviously, he's not dead!

405
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,967
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

406
00:16:30,967 --> 00:16:32,033
So this is just a scheme?

407
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:33,167
Yes!

408
00:16:35,433 --> 00:16:38,167
[MEN CHATTING INDISTINCTLY]

409
00:16:38,167 --> 00:16:40,100
This is one of Django's
gambling spots!

410
00:16:42,633 --> 00:16:44,133
- Come on, let's go!
- We're in his territory!

411
00:16:44,133 --> 00:16:45,267
- Let's go, hurry!
- I'll go now!

412
00:16:45,267 --> 00:16:46,400
You suck at shuffling,
you cheat!

413
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,433
- [MAN] Hey, where's your--
- Aah!

414
00:16:47,433 --> 00:16:48,433
Django!

415
00:16:48,433 --> 00:16:49,800
Surprise!

416
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,700
- It's Django!
- Get them!

417
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:54,733
- Make way!
- Run, hurry!

418
00:16:57,133 --> 00:16:59,567
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

419
00:16:59,567 --> 00:17:00,633
[SEBASTIAN] Hmm?

420
00:17:00,933 --> 00:17:02,900
What's with the serious looks?

421
00:17:02,900 --> 00:17:04,333
Worried about something?

422
00:17:04,333 --> 00:17:06,767
Perhaps the investigation by
the Internal Affairs people?

423
00:17:07,667 --> 00:17:08,833
Hmm?
[SCOFFS LIGHTLY]

424
00:17:08,833 --> 00:17:11,100
Don't worry about that.
It's already taken care of.

425
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:12,767
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

426
00:17:12,767 --> 00:17:14,433
Sir Sebastian is the way!

427
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:16,067
- The way?
- Yes!

428
00:17:16,067 --> 00:17:17,100
Going where?

429
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:18,767
What do you mean?

430
00:17:19,467 --> 00:17:21,400
I've already talked
to Sir Delgado

431
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:24,000
to make sure
you don't lose your job.

432
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,833
So, being the top agent...

433
00:17:26,167 --> 00:17:27,667
I believe he'd listen to me.

434
00:17:28,267 --> 00:17:30,633
So, I got you,
my almost-girlfriend.

435
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,600
[RALLOS] Hear that, guys?

436
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:34,767
Sir Seb saves the day! Right?

437
00:17:34,767 --> 00:17:36,100
Ma'am Sam...

438
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:38,167
How many points
will he get for that?

439
00:17:38,167 --> 00:17:40,233
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

440
00:17:40,233 --> 00:17:41,300
[SAM CHUCKLES DRYLY]

441
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:42,867
Uh, Seb, look...

442
00:17:42,867 --> 00:17:45,067
- My problems....
- [SEBASTIAN] Mmm.

443
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,900
...are mine to handle.
No need to worry about them.

444
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,800
Sam, no way.

445
00:17:49,833 --> 00:17:51,333
I need to be hands-on

446
00:17:51,333 --> 00:17:53,900
with what my almost-girlfriend
is going through.

447
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:55,333
In fact, you know,

448
00:17:55,333 --> 00:17:59,167
I even volunteered
to handle Mr. Chan's transfer.

449
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,000
[SAM, KAREN]
What did you say?

450
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,200
Almost-girlfriend?

451
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,767
Mr. Chan's transfer?

452
00:18:03,967 --> 00:18:04,833
Yes.

453
00:18:05,267 --> 00:18:06,333
And yes.

454
00:18:07,967 --> 00:18:10,767
Unfortunately, Mr. Delgado
turned down my offer.

455
00:18:10,767 --> 00:18:12,533
But, hey-- Don't worry.

456
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:14,300
Sam, just think about this.

457
00:18:14,633 --> 00:18:18,567
The Internal Affairs people
will see that you're the key

458
00:18:18,567 --> 00:18:21,867
to solving this
gold smuggling ring.

459
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:23,200
So, you got this.

460
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,367
And I got you.

461
00:18:24,367 --> 00:18:29,300
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

462
00:18:29,300 --> 00:18:30,333
You got her?

463
00:18:30,767 --> 00:18:32,300
- Sure?
- [RALLOS] I got you.

464
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:33,933
Achoo! That's for you!

465
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:35,733
- Mm-hmm.
- So sticky.

466
00:18:36,667 --> 00:18:37,667
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

467
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:40,300
- Sir.
- [DELGADO] Oh.

468
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:41,267
Sam.

469
00:18:42,133 --> 00:18:43,100
Yes?

470
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:44,233
Come in.

471
00:18:44,233 --> 00:18:46,800
Sir, I heard things blew up here
because of Mr. Chan.

472
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:48,000
[DELGADO] That's right.

473
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,900
However, I think all of that
happened because

474
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:54,433
Victor Zafra's family showed up
here at the police station.

475
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:57,200
I'm pretty sure the only reason
they came here

476
00:18:57,233 --> 00:18:59,167
was to prove they won't fold.

477
00:18:59,633 --> 00:19:00,800
And so, sir...

478
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:02,900
Like I've been telling you,

479
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:05,233
- we need to strengthen the--
- S-Sam...

480
00:19:05,233 --> 00:19:07,367
They are very influential.

481
00:19:07,367 --> 00:19:09,667
They'll use all their money
and all their connections.

482
00:19:09,667 --> 00:19:11,633
They'll do everything to get
their son out of jail.

483
00:19:11,633 --> 00:19:12,733
Sam.

484
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:14,767
Sir.

485
00:19:16,667 --> 00:19:18,200
Never mind, never mind.

486
00:19:18,833 --> 00:19:20,600
[DELGADO SIGHING]

487
00:19:21,933 --> 00:19:25,767
I won't let those things happen.

488
00:19:25,767 --> 00:19:28,967
And I'm not going
to let Tiger go unpunished

489
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,233
for all his sins either.

490
00:19:31,233 --> 00:19:36,533
For now, though,
let us handle this ourselves.

491
00:19:36,533 --> 00:19:39,167
For now, focus...

492
00:19:40,133 --> 00:19:42,633
...on facing
the Internal Affairs.

493
00:19:43,967 --> 00:19:44,967
Please.

494
00:19:53,167 --> 00:19:54,333
[KAREN GASPS] Sam!

495
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:00,733
What did you talk about?

496
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:04,133
Just about Zafra's family
going here.

497
00:20:05,133 --> 00:20:07,833
Sir said I shouldn't bother
with that case anymore.

498
00:20:07,833 --> 00:20:09,533
He said I should think
about my case.

499
00:20:10,467 --> 00:20:14,433
Well, I have a feeling
everything will turn out okay.

500
00:20:15,567 --> 00:20:17,800
You know, Karen,
no matter what happens...

501
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:22,067
Even if I get fired,
you should all still be fine.

502
00:20:22,067 --> 00:20:24,367
Sam, what's with you?
Why are you saying that?

503
00:20:24,367 --> 00:20:27,500
Think positive!
The stars are aligning.

504
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:29,600
You'll have the chance
to explain your side

505
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:30,933
to the higher-ups,

506
00:20:30,933 --> 00:20:33,967
and you'll have the chance
to get a boyfriend.

507
00:20:33,967 --> 00:20:36,733
Huh? You really believe
in that?

508
00:20:36,767 --> 00:20:38,800
He called you
his almost-girlfriend!

509
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:42,067
- Did you disagree with him?
- He said that last night, too.

510
00:20:42,067 --> 00:20:44,700
Again, you did not disagree
with him.

511
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:48,167
- That's not on my mind yet.
- Well, what is in your mind?

512
00:20:48,167 --> 00:20:49,200
Your heart?

513
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:51,000
[KAREN CHUCKLING]

514
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,000
Sorry.

515
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:54,933
Where are you going?

516
00:20:57,100 --> 00:20:58,100
Sam.

517
00:20:59,667 --> 00:21:00,933
[SEBASTIAN CLEARS THROAT]

518
00:21:00,933 --> 00:21:01,967
Um...

519
00:21:01,967 --> 00:21:04,233
I just wanted
to make something clear.

520
00:21:05,100 --> 00:21:06,200
What is it?

521
00:21:08,467 --> 00:21:12,933
Everyone here knows that
you're my almost-girlfriend.

522
00:21:12,933 --> 00:21:15,733
And, as Ariana Grande did say...

523
00:21:16,867 --> 00:21:19,833
Almost is never enough.

524
00:21:19,833 --> 00:21:23,833
So, I want to remove
that "almost" in our label.

525
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:25,467
What do you think?

526
00:21:26,267 --> 00:21:28,500
Seb, we don't really have
a label,

527
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,500
and I have enough problems
as it is.

528
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:32,267
- Can we not do this now?
- Sam!

529
00:21:32,967 --> 00:21:34,033
Can't you see?

530
00:21:35,233 --> 00:21:37,567
I'm the one reducing
your problems!

531
00:21:37,567 --> 00:21:38,533
Really?

532
00:21:39,133 --> 00:21:40,600
But I don't feel it.

533
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:43,000
Well then, I'm going
to make you feel it.

534
00:21:43,033 --> 00:21:45,700
If you're struggling
with your problems...

535
00:21:46,500 --> 00:21:48,767
I can carry them all!

536
00:21:48,767 --> 00:21:51,500
So long as we become a couple.

537
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:53,733
I mean, Sam,
what else is missing?

538
00:21:54,433 --> 00:21:56,700
You already introduced me
to your parents,

539
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:57,867
so, in essence...

540
00:21:59,333 --> 00:22:01,000
We're legal, aren't we?

541
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:02,267
[SAM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

542
00:22:02,267 --> 00:22:04,700
Tomorrow, okay? Tomorrow.
Tomorrow.

543
00:22:04,700 --> 00:22:06,700
We'll officially be a couple
tomorrow? Really?

544
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:07,933
No. Tomorrow--

545
00:22:07,933 --> 00:22:09,800
I'll answer
your question tomorrow.

546
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:13,600
For now, can you give me
just a little bit of peace?

547
00:22:17,833 --> 00:22:18,800
Tomorrow.

548
00:22:20,633 --> 00:22:21,567
Yes!

549
00:22:22,367 --> 00:22:23,367
Tomorrow...

550
00:22:24,833 --> 00:22:25,800
[SEBASTIAN CHUCKLES]

551
00:22:26,467 --> 00:22:28,233
Your smile's too bright.

552
00:22:28,233 --> 00:22:29,533
Like there's
no approaching storm.

553
00:22:30,133 --> 00:22:32,300
The weather app said
we'll have clear skies.

554
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:33,767
[PIA SCOFFS]

555
00:22:33,767 --> 00:22:34,700
Mm-hmm!

556
00:22:39,767 --> 00:22:40,733
Hey.

557
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:43,833
Internal Affairs is here.

558
00:22:44,533 --> 00:22:46,100
You know what you should do.

559
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:49,500
I'm ready to talk with them.
I've been waiting for them.

560
00:22:49,533 --> 00:22:51,467
Wow! We're the same!

561
00:22:51,467 --> 00:22:53,767
Exciting, isn't it?
They're here.

562
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:55,533
Hey, all of you!

563
00:22:56,133 --> 00:22:58,600
Don't forget
you're in this, too.

564
00:22:58,600 --> 00:22:59,667
[PIA SCOFFS]

565
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:03,567
Well, good luck to the others...

566
00:23:07,667 --> 00:23:09,233
And goodbye to you.

567
00:23:11,367 --> 00:23:13,100
[PIA CHUCKLING]

568
00:23:20,267 --> 00:23:22,033
- [CRYING]
- Stop crying.

569
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:24,100
[CRYING]

570
00:23:24,233 --> 00:23:25,600
God won't abandon you.

571
00:23:27,100 --> 00:23:29,233
She will live, I promise.

572
00:23:29,367 --> 00:23:31,100
We should pray for her safety.

573
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,900
Let's find a chapel.

574
00:23:34,033 --> 00:23:41,000
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

575
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:43,533
Come on.

576
00:23:49,633 --> 00:23:56,600
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

577
00:24:11,667 --> 00:24:18,633
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

578
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:24,700
Pochoy...

579
00:24:28,233 --> 00:24:30,067
I know that you're heartbroken
about what happened.

580
00:24:31,233 --> 00:24:32,867
But don't worry.

581
00:24:35,367 --> 00:24:37,200
Because God will always
be with you.

582
00:24:38,933 --> 00:24:41,333
We will pray for your mother.

583
00:24:49,900 --> 00:24:51,633
In the name of the Father,

584
00:24:51,767 --> 00:24:55,133
and of the Son,
and of the Holy Spirit.

585
00:24:55,267 --> 00:24:56,300
Amen.

586
00:24:56,833 --> 00:24:58,033
Lord Jesus,

587
00:24:58,500 --> 00:25:01,167
please heal my mother.

588
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:03,800
Please don't take her away.

589
00:25:04,300 --> 00:25:06,133
I promise,

590
00:25:06,267 --> 00:25:08,700
I will be a nice kid
from now on.

591
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:10,133
[SNIFFLES]

592
00:25:10,267 --> 00:25:17,233
[HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

593
00:25:32,267 --> 00:25:39,233
[HOPEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

594
00:25:51,400 --> 00:25:52,633
You know, Pochoy...

595
00:25:54,167 --> 00:25:56,900
I know the pain
you're feeling right now.

596
00:25:58,133 --> 00:26:02,500
Because my mother died
when I was young.

597
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:05,100
It caused me so much pain.

598
00:26:06,133 --> 00:26:07,900
And I don't want you
to feel that.

599
00:26:11,233 --> 00:26:12,967
But I know, Pochoy...

600
00:26:15,467 --> 00:26:18,700
God will protect Miss Linda.

601
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:21,100
I assure you...

602
00:26:22,433 --> 00:26:24,200
Your mom will be okay.

603
00:26:24,700 --> 00:26:28,233
God will hear your prayer.

604
00:26:29,500 --> 00:26:31,367
And He will not abandon you.

605
00:26:33,533 --> 00:26:35,433
Because God loves you so much.

606
00:26:40,467 --> 00:26:42,100
[GABO] Pops is my only hope.

607
00:26:42,667 --> 00:26:44,433
<i> I hope he'll give me a job.</i>

608
00:26:45,133 --> 00:26:47,400
<i> I need to help Miss Linda.</i>

609
00:26:47,967 --> 00:26:50,867
<i> Pochoy can't lose his mom.</i>

610
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:53,100
<i>I don't want him to feel
what I felt</i>

611
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:55,300
<i> when my mother died.</i>

612
00:26:56,133 --> 00:26:58,233
<i>Agent Jacinto, the state
of your career will depend</i>

613
00:26:58,367 --> 00:26:59,933
<i> on Mr. Chan's testimony.</i>

614
00:27:00,067 --> 00:27:01,733
<i> You were furious</i>

615
00:27:01,867 --> 00:27:03,933
<i>when I hired Betchay
to work in BeerGin.</i>

616
00:27:04,067 --> 00:27:06,033
<i> Now, she's of use to us.</i>

617
00:27:06,167 --> 00:27:10,167
<i>We learned from her
that Gabo received</i>

618
00:27:10,300 --> 00:27:12,933
<i> 200,000 pesos.</i>

619
00:27:13,067 --> 00:27:13,933
<i> Gabo is here.</i>

620
00:27:14,067 --> 00:27:15,133
<i> I need a job.</i>

621
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:16,267
<i> I need money.</i>

622
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:17,300
<i> It doesn't matter</i>

623
00:27:17,433 --> 00:27:19,767
<i>if we don't know
where the money came from.</i>

624
00:27:19,900 --> 00:27:21,933
<i> Django is working on it.</i>

625
00:27:22,067 --> 00:27:23,933
<i>How much do you need
for you to tell me</i>

626
00:27:24,067 --> 00:27:25,400
<i> what Gabo has been up to?</i>

627
00:27:25,533 --> 00:27:28,133
<i>How did he get
the 200,000 pesos?</i>

628
00:27:28,267 --> 00:27:29,967
<i>I thought the time we
spent in prison</i>

629
00:27:30,100 --> 00:27:31,967
<i>was the hardest time
of my life.</i>

630
00:27:32,100 --> 00:27:34,167
<i>But I realized that life
here outside is much harder.</i>

631
00:27:34,300 --> 00:27:36,667
<i>Because you have
to fight every day</i>

632
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:38,000
<i> just to live.</i>
